CS35L41 subsystem ID: select this board's stock OS2.0.4 protection firmware.

`cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"` makes `wm_adsp` request the system-specific
`cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot-10251826.wmfw`. The separate asset repository supplies
that name as a byte-identical alias of the official OS2.0.4 generic stock file,
and maps the four position-specific stock protection `.bin` files to the
system-ID/prefix names requested by the driver.

A static WMFW scan confirms the Halo core and the MAX_LRCLK_DELAY, CAL_R,
CAL_CHECKSUM, CAL_STATUS, CAL_R_SELECTED, CAL_SET_STATUS and CAL_AMBIENT
controls. It does not establish equivalence to the documented 29.85.0 build or
prove hardware compatibility. The subsystem-ID lookup was previously observed
on the unit; these OS2.0.4 firmware payloads still require hardware validation.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -2293,3 +2293,17 @@
 	data-lanes = <0 1>;
 };
 
+
+/*
+ * The OS2.0.4 asset repository installs the byte-identical stock generic
+ * CS35L41 protection image under the system-ID filename requested by wm_adsp.
+ * Static inspection finds the MAX_LRCLK_DELAY and CAL_* controls used by
+ * patch 0004, but does not establish build identity or speaker tuning.
+ * This alias preserves stock bytes; it does not synthesize per-speaker data.
+ * The new OS2.0.4 payload has not been tested on hardware; the DTS property
+ * selects a firmware name and does not prove that the selected image works.
+ */
+&cs35l41_tl { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_tr { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_br { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_bl { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
